# Plan completion review gate

When executing a plan from `docs/implementation/plans/`:

1. Read [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and `.cursor/skills/multi-model-plan-review/SKILL.md`
2. Work on a **feature branch** in the main repo (not a worktree): `git checkout -b feat/<name>` from `main`
3. Phase A: adversarial thermo-nuclear self review — fix findings; hand off only on honest **`Verdict: APPROVED`** (no file on disk)
4. **`Verdict: NOT APPROVED`** means keep working; do not hand off
5. After user feedback: fix **every suggestion (all severities, including low priority)** → quality gate → re-run Phase A if code changed → merge when user directs
6. Merge into `main` and delete the feature branch when the user directs

## Fix-everything policy (Phase A and user feedback)

Implement **all** findings and **all** feedback items — every priority, severity, and label (P0–P2+, Critical/Major/Minor, maintenance smell, low priority, nice-to-have, deferred, 🟡/🟢). **Do not defer** because something looks optional.

**Only exception:** you **explicitly disagree** with a specific item and document why in the Phase A handoff (**Explicit disagreements**). Undocumented skips are forbidden.

**Forbidden:** rubber-stamping APPROVED; APPROVED handoffs with hidden deferrals; merging while any non-disagreed feedback remains open.

See `.cursor/skills/multi-model-plan-review/SKILL.md` for full rules.

**Forbidden:** using a worktree for plan implementation by default.
